(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/main.asl#" :text "Entry of site.wasm: the exports the DOM bridge (web/bridge/boot.js) calls. A wasm32 program cannot read a clock, so the bridge times render and hands the numbers to measured.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/main.asl#update" :text "Delivers message code to aslSite/app/update step with the model the bridge holds, prints the resulting bridge ops and returns the next model.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/main.asl#render" :text "Renders the home document with placeholder stats and returns its byte length; the bridge calls it twice to time a cold and a warm pass.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/main.asl#measured" :text "Prints the ops that show the bridge's cold and warm render timings in the proof section.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/ui/bridge.asl#" :text "The op protocol between site.wasm and the DOM bridge: each Op prints as one ASN form per line (:attr :text :swap :copy :store :after).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/theme.asl#" :text "The design system: one palette table of colour roles with dark and light values, emitted as custom properties for both themes, and every rule of site.css.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/mascot.asl#" :text "The chameleon mark as typed SVG: one outline shared by the themed inline drawing (chameleon, small or large, optionally with body bands) and the standalone favicon (iconSvg).")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/mascot.asl#easterBackdrop" :text "decorative backdrop div (easter-layer) with a perch link to the home page holding the leon mascot and two svg egg streams, left and right")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/mascot.asl#leon" :text "the Leon chameleon mascot node: the leon.webp image (640 by 640) with an overlaid svg of two eyelids and lashes inside a swinging container")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/mascot.asl#tailMark" :text "svg tail logo node with classes 'cham' plus the given size and the tailGrad gradient")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/msg.asl#" :text "The messages a click can send and their integer codes, carried in data-msg attributes.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/layout.asl#" :text "Routes, the document head, the top bar, the footer and the section header primitives every page is assembled from.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/home.asl#" :text "The landing page: the problem, what the language removes, the wire frame, the toolbelt and the proof that the page itself is an ASL program.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/home.asl#installLine" :text "the install command shown on the home page: curl -fsSL https://aslang.dev/install.sh | sh")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/docs.asl#" :text "The language on one page, drawn from llms.txt and the README.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/blog.asl#" :text "The Post record, the blog index, an article page and the 404 page.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/site/app/update.asl#" :text "The pure update: the model is an Int64 whose bit 0 is the light theme and bit 1 an explicit choice; step maps a message and the model to the next model and the bridge ops to apply.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/build.asl#" :text "Builds web/dist: copies web/public and the bridge, compiles web/site/main.asl through asl-target-llvm to site.wasm with llc and wasm-ld and plain-named exports, then prerenders every page, site.css, 404.html, sitemap.xml and rss.xml on the host.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/build.asl#distDir" :text "site output directory for a layout prefix: the prefix followed by web/dist")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/build.asl#layoutPrefix" :text "path prefix from the two layout flags: some asl/ when the workspace layout exists (it wins), some empty string when only the exported layout exists, none otherwise")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/build.asl#prefixIn!" :text "layout prefix of a base directory, from whether asl/web/tools/build.asl (asl/) or web/tools/build.asl (empty) exists under it, none when neither does")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/build.asl#sourceDigest!" :text "sha256 over the digests of the site, bridge, public, content and tools directories, the asl-html sources and llms.txt under the prefix")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/build.asl#stampBridge" :text "the bridge script with fetch of /site.wasm rewritten to carry the ?v=version query")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/build.asl#stampPage" :text "the html with the quoted /site.css, /boot.js and /site.wasm references given a ?v=version query")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/build.asl#webDir" :text "site root directory for a layout prefix: the prefix followed by web")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/posts.asl#" :text "Reads web/content/blog/index.asn with asl-parser/reader and each post body from web/content/blog/<slug>.md into published Posts, newest first.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tools/feeds.asl#" :text "sitemap.xml and rss.xml rendered from the routes and posts through the same Node serializer.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tests/siteTest.asl#" :text "Serializer escaping, CSS rendering, the bridge encoding, the update transitions and the prerendered home document.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tests/buildLayoutTest.asl#runTests" :text "SITE-BUILD-EXPORT-LAYOUT gate: the build prefix is asl/ under the workspace layout, empty under the exported layout and none for a directory with neither, the workspace layout wins when both exist, stampPage and stampBridge add the build version query, and webDir and distDir for both prefixes")
(:doc :symbol "asl/web/tests/distFreshTest.asl#runTests" :text "site dist freshness gate: the sources digest is 64 characters and the committed web/dist/build.asn records exactly that digest, so a stale dist is red until rebuilt")
